llow users to view\nanalytics for specific time periods instead of being limited to all historical\ndata.\n\nFrontend Changes (analytics/+page.svelte):\n- Added date range filter UI with show/hide toggle\n- Quick preset buttons: Last 7 Days, Last 30 Days, Last 90 Days, Last Year\n- Custom date range selector with start and end date inputs\n- Date validation (end date cannot be before start date)\n- Filter state persists when selecting different competitors\n- Responsive design for mobile devices\n\nAPI Layer Changes (lib/api.js):\n- Updated getAnalyticsOverview() to accept query parameters\n- Updated getCompetitorAnalytics() to accept query parameters\n- Updated getAllCompetitors() to accept query parameters\n- All functions now support start_date and end_date filtering\n\nBackend Changes (orchestrator/app/main.py):\n- Added start_date and end_date query parameters to:\n  * GET /analytics/overview\n  * GET /analytics/competitor/{competitor_name}\n  * GET /analytics/competitors/list\n- Date filters applied to both Job and SentimentResult tables\n- Inclusive date filtering (includes entire end date)\n- Input validation with helpful error messages\n- Filters applied consistently across all queries\n\nFeatures:\n- Filter by custom date range (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n- Quick preset options for common time periods\n- Real-time data updates when filters change\n- Clear visual indication of active date range\n- All analytics metrics respect the date filter\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0350e8d9a9bc3b327a7be8ac1bcc0aa780a522ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/trees/0350e8d9a9bc3b327a7be8ac1bcc0aa780a522ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/commits/f84477353994cba39322dd14e539b6715e0d6baf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135322706?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1","id":135322706,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commit/f84477353994cba39322dd14e539b6715e0d6baf","node_id":"C_kwDOQBoD2toAKGY4NDQ3NzM1Mzk5NGNiYTM5MzIyZGQxNGU1MzliNjcxNWUwZDZiYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commit/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb","sha":"0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb"}],"sha":"f84477353994cba39322dd14e539b6715e0d6baf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/f84477353994cba39322dd14e539b6715e0d6baf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135322706?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1","id":135322706,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-20T11:05:21Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-20T11:05:21Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"message":"Add OpenAI API support as alternative to local Llama model\n\nAdded the option to use OpenAI''s API instead of the local Llama 2 model for\nsentiment analysis. Users can now choose between:\n- \"llama\": Local Llama 2 7B model (default, no API key required)\n- \"openai\": OpenAI API (requires OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable)\n\nChanges:\n- Added openai package to requirements.txt\n- Created analyze_sentiment_with_openai() and analyze_sentiment_with_llama()\n  helper functions to separate the logic\n- Updated analyze_contextual_sentiment() to support model selection via\n  SENTIMENT_MODEL environment variable\n- Added SENTIMENT_MODEL, OPENAI_API_KEY, and OPENAI_MODEL_NAME environment\n  variables to docker-compose.yml (defaults: llama, empty, gpt-4o-mini)\n- Updated .env and .env.example files with new configuration options\n\nBenefits:\n- OpenAI API provides faster response times and potentially better accuracy\n- No need to download and store large model files when using OpenAI\n- Flexibility to switch between local and cloud-based models\n- Same prompt and sentiment classification logic for both models\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd7d4069ccdfd025c65754575505c4f4c1214a9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/trees/dd7d4069ccdfd025c65754575505c4f4c1214a9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/commits/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135322706?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1","id":135322706,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commit/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb","node_id":"C_kwDOQBoD2toAKDBkYmM1OWVlNjZkYmFlY2Q5NGY5NTc2YmM1NTlhM2MwMjE4MzExYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commit/1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce","sha":"1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce"}],"sha":"0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/0dbc59ee66dbaecd94f9576bc559a3c0218311bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135322706?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1","id":135322706,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-20T10:58:57Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-20T10:58:57Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"message":"Improve LLM prompt to correctly classify neutral statements\n\nEnhanced the LLM prompt with specific rules and examples to better identify\nneutral statements such as factual information, introductions, and\nidentification statements (e.g., \"calling from Three\", \"this is EE\").\n\nThe LLM now understands that only emotional or evaluative statements about\nthe context should be classified as positive or negative, while factual\nstatements should be classified as neutral.\n\nThis fixes the issue where statements like \"Gabe from three\" were being\nincorrectly classified as positive instead of neutral.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a59105f3f82fe8feb86f5a4f33d56571dc34b90b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/trees/a59105f3f82fe8feb86f5a4f33d56571dc34b90b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/commits/1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135322706?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1","id":135322706,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commit/1baf9e133b67eeed609a0b1836df3cf27499e3ce","node