06,"login":"jjwoods1","node_id":"U_kgDOCBDcUg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjwoods1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/commits/d0b07d44bfbf5c306e425520a4e65841d4668ac6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-14T14:35:10Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-14T14:35:10Z","email":"jjwoods1@icloud.com","name":"Jaidon Woods"},"message":"Fix multi-competitor sentiment analysis and add 30-min timeout protection\n\n- Fix Celery chain logic to process all competitors sequentially\n  - Modified analyze_sentiment_for_competitor to accept previous_result parameter\n  - Updated return value to pass context dict to next task in chain\n  - Fixed process_sentiment_analysis to properly initialize chain with job_id\n\n- Add automatic timeout protection for stuck jobs\n  - Created check_stuck_jobs periodic task (runs every 5 minutes)\n  - Marks jobs as FAILED if processing for >30 minutes\n  - Revokes all related Celery tasks using SIGKILL\n  - Sends failure notifications for timed-out jobs\n\n- Configure Celery Beat schedule for periodic timeout checks\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"819663bea1f506912de36d1c649cc9cee7b91dd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservice-architecture/git/trees/819663bea1f506912de36d1c649cc9cee7b91dd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jjwoods1/sentiment-analysis-microservic